/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  layoutDict -- the PLOT PLAN of the apalutamide tablet plant (DEV.md 4c C97,
  rearranged in C100).  A STARTING POINT for the group, to copy and change.

  WHAT STANDS WHERE, AND WHY.  A spray-dried dispersion of a potent API is
  made INSIDE the GMP building, never on a platform in the rain: the solution
  is prepared, sprayed and dried in contained, classified rooms the people
  reach through airlocks, and the dried powder goes straight to the
  granulation train next door.  So every process item of this plant stands
  in a ROOM of the `building {}` at the end of this file (each room's
  `equipment ( ... )` lists it; its base is the room's floor, so no item
  indoors declares a `z`):
    * the spray dryer, in a double-height, contained SPRAY-DRYING SUITE on
      the north wall, its explosion vent ducted out through that wall;
    * the solution tank, in a contained SOLUTION-PREPARATION room;
    * the closed nitrogen loop -- gas heater, blower, exhaust cooler, solvent
      condenser, condensate pot -- in a TECHNICAL room beside the suite, on
      the outside wall, reached from outside for maintenance;
    * the coating-suspension tank, in a preparation room beside the coater;
    * the coating air heater, in the air-handling plant on the technical
      floor, above the coating room.
  What industry keeps OUTDOORS stays outdoors: the BULK SOLVENT -- a fresh-
  acetone tank and a recovered-acetone tank -- in a bunded tank farm east of
  the building, downwind of it, its pipes carried on a short rack across the
  east road and into the building through its east wall.  Beside them, the
  site buildings as NON-PROCESS items: the offices and quality-control
  laboratory by the gate, and the warehouse.

  WHAT IS THE ENGINE'S AND WHAT IS OURS.  The spray dryer's chamber and the
  three vessels' diameters and heights are their sizers' own; the
  exchangers, the blower and the tanks publish an AREA, a POWER or a
  VOLUME, not a shape, so their plan boxes are DECLARED below (each with
  the arithmetic).  EVERYTHING ELSE IS AN AUTHOR-SET ASSUMPTION FOR THE
  GROUP TO REPLACE WITH ITS OWN SITE DATA: every position, every building's
  size, every separation distance, the wind and every hazardous-area zone.
  They are round numbers chosen so that the checks are visible on this
  plant, not values from any spacing or hazardous-area standard: the
  published ones (IEC 60079-10-1 and its national codes for zones; company
  and insurance spacing guides) grant no redistribution, and a citation
  invented for a round number would turn "unsourced" into "falsely sourced".

  THE BUND.  The two tanks are meant to stand in one bund -- a low wall
  round the farm that holds a spill.  A bund is a DECLARED REGION of this
  file since DEV.md 4c C134 (`bunds ( { name; kind bund; items ( ... );
  region { ... } wall { height; } capacityRule { ... } drain; ... } )`,
  held by the engine to the capacity rule the case states and cites), and
  none is declared here: the run ANNOUNCES both tanks as liquid stores no
  containment encloses (`unbundedLiquid`).  Declaring it -- its wall, its
  rule (at least the larger tank, plus rainwater) and its source -- is the
  group's.

  ONE FINDING IS LEFT ON PURPOSE: the site has ONE entrance (`singleEntrance`,
  read the README, section 7).  And one question the engine does NOT check,
  left for the group: the spray dryer's EXPLOSION VENT discharges through
  the north wall of its suite, 1 m from the paved edge of the north road --
  how large is the vent, how far does the flame and the pressure reach, and
  may that road stay where it is while the dryer runs?

  PIPES INDOORS ARE NOT DRAWN.  The router draws pipes in the open only: a
  stream whose two ends stand indoors is listed as "inside the building:
  indoor piping is not routed", and a stream with one end indoors is drawn
  only where this file DECLARES its outdoor leg up to the WALL PENETRATION
  (`pipes` below: the acetone in, the recovered acetone out).  The nitrogen
  make-up (from a supply this case does not model) and the purge (to a vent
  treatment it does not model) are listed with that reason.  SOLIDS ARE NOT
  PIPED either: the bought powders, the dispersion, the blends, granules and
  tablet cores are listed as "solids only, moved in containers or by
  conveyor".  See the README (section 7).

  Grammar and checks: docs/design/a-plant-layout-is-declared-and-checked.md
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

